From b810ab644040fb8b13da72a407ce0bb732fd4534 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivel=C3=A4?=
 <5814559+villekivela@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:07:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] extensions: let an extension create an offscreen document

chrome.offscreen.createDocument took the browser down, every time. An
offscreen document lives in contents the extension system creates
itself, with no WebContentsAdapter, so WebContentsViewQt has no factory
client and every RenderWidgetHostViewQt in those contents is made
without a delegate. The document's first navigation creates a
speculative main frame, and RenderFrameHostManager::
CreateSpeculativeRenderFrame hides that frame's view. Hide() asserted a
delegate in debug builds and dereferenced the null one in release.

ShowWithVisibility() already handles the missing delegate by deferring
the show to setDelegate(). Hide() now does the same: it hides the
delegate when there is one and otherwise cancels a deferred show, so a
delegate that arrives later does not show a view Chromium hid.
IsShowing() answers false without a delegate.

Bitwarden creates an offscreen document, and that is how this was
found: the browser crashed on resume from suspend (villekivela/omaweb#646).
Stock QtWebEngine 6.11.2 crashes the same way, and dev and 6.140 have
the same Hide().

The test creates an offscreen document from an extension page and waits
for the document to message back. Without the fix the test program
dies with SIGSEGV in RenderWidgetHostViewQt::Hide().
